ttempt\",\"Confirmed outbound HTTPS reachability to vault.centos.org (CentOS7-compatible mirror)\",\"Downloaded aide-0.15.1-13.el7.x86_64.rpm from vault.centos.org and installed it via rpm -ivh\",\"Reviewed /etc/aide.conf: default RHEL7 config already applies a recursive PERMS rule across all of /etc plus CONTENT_EX (SHA256+perms) rules for dozens of critical /etc subpaths/files\",\"Ran 'aide --init' to build the initial database, then copied aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz to activate it as the baseline\",\"Ran 'aide --check' confirming a clean baseline ('All files match AIDE database')\",\"Appended a line to /etc/issue (a tracked file) and re-ran 'aide --check', confirming AIDE detected the SHA256 change (exit code 4, 1 changed file) - proving the baseline can identify later /etc changes\",\"Reverted the /etc/issue change and re-ran 'aide --check' to confirm baseline returned to clean\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id, uptime -s, and aide.db.gz md5sum as the healthy baseline\",\"Issued 'shutdown -r now' via nohup/background so the ack returned before disconnect\",\"Polled node1 until SSH connectivity returned\",\"Captured post-restart boot_id (changed) and uptime -s (new boot time) as proof of an actual restart\",\"Re-verified aide.db.gz md5sum unchanged and re-ran 'aide --check' post-restart confirming baseline persisted and integrity checking still functions cleanly\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"AIDE integrity tool installed and baseline database initialized for /etc coverage on node1\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-58483c7d28634df4\",\"cmd-15e411f028d64cf2\",\"cmd-da9bbfcbb8b7491f\",\"cmd-89c341051fe5412c\",\"cmd-ad5e3fe172fc4bd1\",\"cmd-14d33d3973214280\",\"cmd-08b5f72312924d12\"],\"summary\":\"node1 had no aide package and no enabled yum repos; downloaded compatible RHEL7 rpm from vault.centos.org, installed via rpm, confirmed default aide.conf covers /etc with a tree-wide PERMS rule plus CONTENT_EX/SHA256 rules for critical config files, ran aide --init, and activated the resulting database as aide.db.gz\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline correctly validates clean state and detects later changes to /etc\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-94a0297445404292\",\"cmd-59a4ad8575204b9a\",\"cmd-6c2c6120b8e34117\",\"cmd-1449272c1c7c4951\"],\"summary\":\"Initial aide --check reported 'All files match AIDE database' (clean). After appending text to the tracked file /etc/issue, aide --check exited 4 and reported 1 changed file with the differing SHA256 hashes, proving detection works. After reverting, aide --check returned to clean, confirming the baseline is intact and usable going forward\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory node1 restart: healthy pre-restart baseline captured\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a4feb5885e66415d\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id 325732f1-bc39-4512-b05e-397f42060246, uptime start 2026-09-29 10:24:12, aide.db.gz md5sum be6e20e2..., and a clean aide --check result immediately before restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory node1 restart: acknowledged restart and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-0182771d2b534bac\",\"cmd-0ce6c33ccd1c42e2\",\"cmd-fa4cf71db5c94440\",\"cmd-5c2bdd1a3f294590\"],\"summary\":\"Issued 'shutdown -r now' in the background so the exec call acknowledged before disconnect; subsequent polls timed out (node down) then succeeded with a new boot_id 0149bfc8-b11a-4d5b-82e3-e834ebf7c1c9 and new uptime start 10:31:17, proving an actual reboot occurred (not just a service restart)\"},{\"requirement\":\"Mandatory node1 restart: post-restart recovery of integrity baseline verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c7392293efe34422\"],\"summary\":\"After restart, aide.db.gz md5sum matched the pre-restart value exactly and aide --check again reported 'All files match AIDE database', confirming the /etc integrity baseline survived the restart and remains fully functional\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Established an AIDE-based file integrity baseline for /etc on node1 (RHEL 7.9), verified it detects and clears changes correctly, then completed the mandatory single-node restart protocol with boot-identity and recovery proof.","actions_performed":["Inspected node1 (RHEL 7.9, no aide installed, no yum repos enabled)","Cleared a stale yum lock left by a prior timed-out install attempt","Confirmed outbound HTTPS reachability to vault.centos.org (CentOS7-compatible mirror)","Downloaded aide-0.15.1-13.el7.x86_64.rpm from vault.centos.org and installed it via rpm -ivh","Reviewed /etc/aide.conf: default RHEL7 config already applies a recursive PERMS rule across all of /etc plus CONTENT_EX (SHA256+perms) rules for dozens of critical /etc subpaths/files","Ran 'aide --init' to build the initial database, then copied aide.db.new.gz to aide.db.gz to activate it as the baseline","Ran 'aide --check' confirming a clean baseline ('All files match AIDE database')","Appended a line to /etc/issue (a tracked file) and re-ran 'aide --check', confirming AIDE detected the SHA256 change (exit code 4, 1 changed file) - proving the baseline can identify later /etc changes","Reverted the /etc/issue change and re-ran 'aide --check' to confirm baseline returned to clean","Captured pre-restart boot_id, uptime -s, and aide.db.gz md5sum as the healthy baseline","Issued 'shutdown -r now' via nohup/background so the ack returned before disconnect","Polled node1 until SSH connectivity returned","Captured post-restart boot_id (changed) and uptime -s (new boot time) as proof of an actual restart","Re-verified aide.db.gz md5sum unchanged and re-ran 'aide --check' post-restart confirming baseline persisted and integrity checking still functions cleanly"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"AIDE integrity tool installed and baseline database initialized for /etc coverage on node1","command_ids":["cmd-58483c7d28634df4","cmd-15e411f028d64cf2","cmd-da9bbfcbb8b7491f","cmd-89c341051fe5412c","cmd-ad5e3fe172fc4bd1","cmd-14d33d3973214280","cmd-08b5f72312924d12"],"summary":"node1 had no aide package and no enabled yum repos; downloaded compatible RHEL7 rpm from vault.centos.org, installed via rpm, confirmed default aide.conf covers /etc with a tree-wide PERMS rule plus CONTENT_EX/SHA256 rules for critical config files, ran aide --init, and activated the resulting database as aide.db.gz"},{"requirement":"Baseline correctly validates clean state and detects later changes to /etc","command_ids":["cmd-94a0297445404292","cmd-59a4ad8575204b9a","cmd-6c2c6120b8e34117","cmd-1449272c1c7c4951"],"summary":"Initial aide --check reported 'All files match AIDE database' (clean). After appending text to the tracked file /etc/issue, aide --check exited 4 and reported 1 changed file with the differing SHA256 hashes, proving detection works. After reverting, aide --check returned to clean, confirming the baseline is intact and usable going forward"},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart: healthy pre-restart baseline captured","command_ids":["cmd-a4feb5885e66415d"],"summary":"Captured boot_id 325732f1-bc39-4512-b05e-397f42060246, uptime start 2026-09-29 10:24:12, aide.db.gz md5sum be6e20e2..., and a clean aide --check result immediately before restart"},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart: acknowledged restart and changed boot identity","command_ids":["cmd-0182771d2b534bac","cmd-0ce6c33ccd1c42e2","cmd-fa4cf71db5c94440","cmd-5c2bdd1a3f294590"],"summary":"Issued 'shutdown -r now' in the background so the exec call acknowledged before disconnect; subsequent polls timed out (node down) then succeeded with a new boot_id 0149bfc8-b11a-4d5b-82e3-e834ebf7c1c9 and new uptime start 10:31:17, proving an actual reboot occurred (not just a service restart)"},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart: post-restart recovery of integrity baseline verified","command_ids":["cmd-c7392293efe34422"],"summary":"After restart, aide.db.gz md5sum matched the pre-restart value exactly and aide --check again reported 'All files match AIDE database', confirming the /etc integrity baseline survived the restart and remains fully functional"}]},"ttft_ms":1491,"type":"result","duration_ms":390098,"uuid":"27d02e1d-4abe-4fd4-bbcd-d33d97abd33d","ttft_stream_ms":972,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":972,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
